    "answer": {
      "short": "Highest to lowest: School C, School A, School B.\n\nConvert each proportion to a percentage before comparing.",
      "worked": "School A:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{7}\\times100\\%&=\\frac{200}{7}\\%\\\\\\frac{2}{7}\\times100\\%&=28\\frac{4}{7}\\%\\end{align*}$$\nSchool B:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{110}{400}\\times100\\%&=\\frac{55}{2}\\%\\\\\\frac{110}{400}\\times100\\%&=27.5\\%\\end{align*}$$\nSchool C: $28.9\\%$.\n\nSince $28.9\\%>28\\frac{4}{7}\\%>27.5\\%$, the ranking from highest to lowest is School C, School A, School B.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
